# Vercel runs only the Python function in api/index.py (see vercel.json) and
# serves the pre-built frontend bundle from backend/app/templates/. Everything
# below is source that is already compiled, or material the deployment never
# reads. Excluding it keeps the upload and the function bundle small.
#
# Do NOT add a blanket "*.md" rule: backend/prompts/agent_skill.md and
# backend/prompts/chat_system_prompt.md are loaded at runtime by
# chat_engine.py and settings_service.py.

.git
.github
.venv
venv
node_modules

# Documentation and developer tooling
docs
scripts
AGENTS.md
CHANGELOG.md
SECURITY.md
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
CITATION.cff
AUTHORS.md
license-policy.json
pyproject.toml
.python-version

# Tests (no test runs in the deployed function)
backend/tests
engine/tests
frontend/tests

# Engine documentation only; engine/ itself is imported by the backend
engine/docs

# Frontend sources: the deployed UI is the pre-built bundle already committed
# under backend/app/templates/. The Textual TUI under frontend/ is a separate
# desktop client that the serverless function never imports.
frontend
